<title>JAPAN: TIFFE euroyen ends sharply down on Nikkei's surge.</title>
<headline>TIFFE euroyen ends sharply down on Nikkei's surge.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>May 6 settlement  prev settlement</p>
<p> TIFFE Euroyen 3M (Z)     98.94		   99.01</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Key December three-month euroyen deposit rate futures ended Tuesday's TIFFE day session sharply lower due to a surge in Tokyo stocks and a sharp fall in Japanese government bond (JGB) futures.</p>
<p>The key contract settled at 98.94 after falling as low as 98.92. Day session turnover was a heavy 101,714 lots.</p>
<p>&quot;Euroyen futures dropped sharply as the Nikkei rose above 20,000,&quot; said a city bank trader.</p>
</text>
